            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 89-year-old female patient, admitted on 22/10/2019 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, pulse oximetry, and blood tests, confirming an acute COPD exacerbation without evidence of pneumonia or cardiac decompensation. The patient was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, leading to satisfactory clinical improvement. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout the stay. She was discharged on 23/10/2019 in stable condition. I recommend continuation of optimised inhaler therapy and close follow-up in your practice. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
